      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To clarify further:\n\nAvatar controllers can tell if you're in a station.\n\nA station itself can check if a player is seated on it.\n\nWhat we don't have is a way for Udon to derive from a player if they are seated.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-13T14:42:00.358Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basically this would be useful to track whether the player is indeed in a station or not; We cannot tell if the player is in an avatar chair; therefore it may break or we had to find another way to let the world instance know that you're no longer in that chair.\n\nI would suggest that it would return either a bool or a gameobject (avatars will return null) when calling something like bool = VRCPlayerAPI.IsPlayerInStation()\n\nor gameobject = VRCPlayerApi.GetCurrentStation",
